{"lyrics":"[00:00.06][Intro: Eric Idle,\n[00:00.40]Young Thug\n[00:00.70]&\n[00:00.76]Tommy Genesis\n[00:01.18]]\n[00:01.24]Some people say it's folly, but I'd rather have the lolly\n[00:03.48]With money, you can make a smash\n[00:05.98]There is nothing quite as wonderful as money, money, money, money\n[00:09.70]There is nothing like a newly minted pound\n[00:11.54](Money, money, money, money)\n[00:13.10]Everyone must hanker for the butchness of a banker\n[00:15.84]It's accountancy that makes the world go 'round, 'round, 'round, 'round\n[00:19.44]You can keep your Marxist ways, for it's only just a phase (Ah, ah, ah, ah)\n[00:26.04]Money, money, money makes the world go 'round\n[00:27.74](\n[00:27.80]Who made the beat? Charlie\n[00:28.50]) (\n[00:28.64]Yee\n[00:28.74])\n[Chorus: Young Thug & Juice WRLD]\n[00:28.82]Monte Carlo, big sharks on my ankles (Monte Carlo)\n[00:30.40]I drape out all my broads, Cartier bangles (Cartier bangles)\n[00:32.16]I go military boys with the angles (Grrah-grrah-grrah, phew-phew)\n[00:34.18]Gotta upgrade the stars, outer space for me (Yeah)\n[00:35.76]'Lotta blue cash in a rubber band (A lotta blue cash in the rubber)\n[00:37.54]Mount it—, she in Barbie land (She in Barbie land)\n[00:39.22]Tropicana diamonds, rock 'em by the tens (By the tens)\n[00:41.02]I'm just drinkin' Act', Kurt Cobain (\n[00:42.84]Uh\n[00:42.88])\n[Verse 1: Juice WRLD & Young Thug]\n[00:42.96]Fresh to death, Gucci on my tomb\n[00:43.98]My chopper sing, it need autotune\n[00:44.80]Bad bitch in my hotel room\n[00:46.18]Take a Perky right before we fuck, then act a fool (\n[00:47.62]Fool\n[00:47.80])\n[00:47.86]Sad money, I got blue face diamonds\n[00:49.00]I'm at the top, and I'ma keep on climbin'\n[00:49.92]I got a **** on my hip, no silence\n[00:50.78]My mama told me, \"Don't trust nobody\"\n[00:51.74]Damn, mama, you seen it comin' (Woo)\n[00:52.68]That's why I don't keep this heat for nothin'\n[00:54.22]Try me, then you're gettin' one (On God)\n[00:55.22]Plus one